-- Phase 7 Task 3, part 2 of 2 — seed the eight "Standard" templates (design spec §9).
--
-- One DocumentTemplate per TemplateDocType, named "Standard", isDefault, with a v1 PUBLISHED
-- DocumentTemplateVersion whose config is that type's DEFAULT_CONFIG
-- (erp/src/lib/template-contracts/) serialized as a JSON literal. The TS constants are the
-- canonical copy; tests/template-seed.test.ts is the drift guard that parses THIS file's
-- dollar-quoted literals (never the live DB — truncateAll() re-seeds from the same constants,
-- which would make a DB assertion a tautology) and deep-equals them per type.
--
-- The four standing-text blocks (cert_statement on CERT; shipper_liability_text on BOTH SHIPPER
-- and MOS_SHIPPER; quote_intro_text and quote_liability_text on QUOTE) are copied from the live
-- "Setting" rows where present — jsonb_set + COALESCE with the code default as the fallback —
-- so a fresh install and an upgraded one both come out right (Setting.value is jsonb, so the
-- COALESCE operates on jsonb string values directly). quote_liability_text's fallback is
-- deliberately '""': a PRESENT key holding the empty string, never an absent key — the builder
-- omits the strip when blank, so the empty default IS today's paper.
--
-- The Setting rows are NOT deleted here and settings.ts is untouched: the print paths still
-- read them until their conversions land (Tasks 9/11/14); retirement completes in Task 14 — the
-- plan's deliberate timing refinement of spec §9 (deleting now would silently revert
-- owner-edited standing texts for the rest of the branch).
--
-- Ids are fixed readable literals (the BillingConfig 'singleton' precedent for
-- migration-seeded rows): standard-<doctype> / standard-<doctype>-v1. publishedById stays NULL —
-- no User row is guaranteed to exist at migrate time; the seeded versions are born published
-- (spec §4.1), so publishedVersionId is pointed at v1 as soon as the row exists.

